  "comment": "The one place that pins the kernel's toolchain (read by crates/eukhe-core/src/kernel/bootstrap/toolchain.rs, embedded in the binary). uv: the release Eukhe downloads into its own directory; sha256 of each release archive (the release's published checksums; Linux uses the static musl build, which runs on every Linux). python: the one CPython every kernel runs on, on every machine; `downloads` is uv's python-downloads list (`uv python install --python-downloads-json-url`), so uv checks the archive against this sha256 before it installs. To move a pin: change the version, the urls and every sha256 (python-build-standalone's SHA256SUMS; uv's <archive>.sha256), set `requires-python` in pyproject.toml to the same minor, then `make runtime-lock`.",
